<Base title="Privacy & saved trips" description="How Ula handles your browser-saved trip brief and downloads.">
<PageHeading label="YOUR DEVICE. YOUR PLANS." title="Your trip stays with you." description="A clear explanation of the personal trip brief and the information this demo stores."/><section class="policy-copy wrap"><h2>What the planner saves</h2><p>When you create a brief, Ula can store your selected destination, route, travel date, traveler group and preferred pace in this browser. It uses local storage so the form can restore your choices on this device.</p><h2>What happens when you download</h2><p>The text file is created in your browser. No trip request is sent to a travel agent, and no booking is made. The downloaded file remains wherever you choose to save it.</p><h2>Clear your saved choices</h2><p>Use the button below to remove the planner's saved choices from this browser. It does not delete files you have already downloaded.</p><button class="button" id="clear-storage"><span>Clear my saved trip brief</span></button><p id="storage-status" role="status"></p><h2>External websites</h2><p>Tourism and transport links open websites with their own privacy practices. Ula's trip planner does not share your saved brief with those sites.</p><p class="demo-note">This page describes the current portfolio demo. Hosting providers may process ordinary request logs according to their own policies.</p></section>
</Base>
